### Prerequisites
- C++11 or later compiler
- Google Test framewrok (for running test)

### Building
```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone <https://github.com/HuyVoDinh/Algorithm.git>

# Compile the example
g++ -std=c++11 example/linkedlist/single-linked-list-sample.cpp -o single-linkedd-list-sample

# Run the example
./single-linked-list-sample
```
## Getting Started

### Including in Your Project
```cpp
#include "linkedlist/SingleLinkedList.cpp"

// For double linkedlist
#include "linkedlist/DoubleLinkedList.cpp"
```

### Testing

This library includes comprehensive tests using Google Test framework

### Running Tests
```bash
#Compile tests
g++ -std=c++17 tests/linkedlist/test_singlelinkedlist.cpp -Iinclude -Igoogletest/googletest/include -Lgoogletest/build/lib -lgtest -lgtest_main -pthread -o build/test_singlelinkedlist.exe

# Run test
.\build\test_singlelinkedlist.exe
```

### Test Coverage
- Basic functionality test
- Edge case tests (empty lists, single elements)
- Exception management test
- Copy semantics tests

### Development Guidelines
- Follow C++11 standards
- Write comprehensive tests for new features
- Maintain existing code style
- Document all public APIs
- Ensure memory safety

---
**Note**: This library is designed for educational purposes and algorithmic practice. For production use, consider using standard library containers like `std::vector`, `std::list`, `std::forward_list`